# Float rewrites: derived, not sampled. Default is within Vulkan precision.
simplify float nofile
```spv
%a = OpFDiv %float %x %float_3_0
OpStore %out %a
```
# Bit-exact mode: a divide by a power of two is an exact scaling.
simplify float exact nofile
```spv
%a = OpFDiv %float %x %float_2_0
OpStore %out %a
```
# A requested ulp budget: a 1-ulp rewrite meets ulp 2.
simplify float ulp 2 nofile
```spv
%a = OpFDiv %float %x %float_3_0
OpStore %out %a
```
# ulp 0 rejects the non-bit-exact multiply.
simplify float ulp 0 nofile
```spv
%a = OpFDiv %float %x %float_3_0
OpStore %out %a
```
# A float range assumption narrows where a rewrite is derived.
simplify float c in [0.1, 10] nofile
```spv
%a = OpExtInst %float %glsl Pow %c %float_2_0
OpStore %out %a
```
